---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../site.config.js';
---
<Base title="Docs: Install AI Assist" description="Install and configure AI Assist in your Salesforce org.">
  <section class="section-sm">
    <div class="container docs-layout">
      <nav class="docs-nav" aria-label="Docs">
        <span class="docs-nav-title">Docs</span>
        <a href="#install" aria-current="page">Getting started</a>
        <a href="#configure">Configuration</a>
        <a href="#commands">Slash commands</a>
        <a href="#pii">PII rules</a>
        <a href="#troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</a>
      </nav>

      <article class="prose">
        <span class="breadcrumb">Docs › Getting started</span>
        <h1 id="install" style="font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.6rem)">Install AI Assist</h1>
        <p>About 20 minutes. You'll need System Administrator access and an API key from Anthropic or OpenAI.</p>

        <ol>
          <li><strong>Install the package.</strong> From AppExchange, choose <em>Install for Admins Only</em>. We recommend a sandbox first.</li>
          <li><strong>Add your AI provider key.</strong> In Setup, open Named Credentials and edit the AI Assist credential.</li>
          <li><strong>Assign permission sets.</strong> Give admins <em>AI Assist Admin</em> and everyone else <em>AI Assist User</em>.</li>
          <li><strong>Add it to a record page.</strong> In Lightning App Builder, drag the AI Assist component onto the page, then save and activate.</li>
          <li><strong>Accept the terms.</strong> The first admin to open AI Assist accepts the Loom Connect terms on behalf of your organisation.</li>
        </ol>

        <div class="callout">Before going live, review which fields count as personal data in AI Assist Setup › PII rules.</div>

        <h2 id="configure">Configuration</h2>
        <p>[Content to come: choosing a model, data sources, agents and retention settings.]</p>

        <h2 id="commands">Slash commands</h2>
        <p>[Content to come: built-in commands and creating your own from prompt templates.]</p>

        <h2 id="pii">PII rules</h2>
        <p>[Content to come: how fields are classified, compliance groups and masking rules.]</p>

        <h2 id="troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</h2>
        <p>[Content to come: common errors and fixes.] Still stuck? <a href="/support">Raise a support request</a> or email <a href={`mailto:${site.email.support}`}>{site.email.support}</a>.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
